{"name":"a11y-checker.md","path":"jsdocs/shared/scripts/verify/a11y-checker.md","format":"markdown","html":"<article class=\"docs-md\"><h1 id=\"sharedscriptsverifya11y-checkermjs\"><code>shared\\scripts\\verify\\a11y-checker.mjs</code></h1>\n<table><thead><tr><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td><strong>Source</strong></td><td><code>src/shared\\scripts\\verify\\a11y-checker.mjs</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>UX surface</strong></td><td>Boot surfaces: what the user sees first on each bundle.</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2 id=\"members\">Members</h2>\n<h3 id=\"gating_levels\"><code>GATING_LEVELS</code></h3>\n<p>Levels that gate the run when not covered by the reviewed baseline.</p>\n<h3 id=\"fingerprintkey\"><code>fingerprintKey</code></h3>\n<p>Stable fingerprint KEY for one finding — rule + positional-index-free\nDOM path. The engine's <code>path.dom</code>/<code>xpath</code> carries <code>[n]</code> sibling\nindices; on pages whose DOM is not fully deterministic at settle\n(playground HUD rows, media-ladder rungs, engine boot timing) the\nindices flap between runs and exact-path baselining would flag the\nsame verified issue as \"new\" forever. Stripping indices keeps the\nelement-type chain; the occurrence ordinal appended by\n<code>fingerprints()</code> keeps N identical-shape siblings distinct, so an\nEXTRA occurrence of a baselined shape still fails the gate.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>@param</code> {object} f finding entry from the checker report</li>\n<li><code>@returns</code> {string} normalized rule+path key (pre-ordinal)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"fingerprints\"><code>fingerprints</code></h3>\n<p>Fingerprints one route's findings: <code>${key}|${ordinal}</code> where ordinal\nis the 0-based occurrence index of that key on the route. Gating\nlevels only — recommendations/manual prompts never block.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>@param</code> {Array<object>} findings raw findings for one route</li>\n<li><code>@returns</code> {Array&lt;{f: object, fp: string}&gt;} finding + fingerprint pairs</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"mime\"><code>MIME</code></h3>\n<p>MIME table for the loopback dist server — only what emitted pages load.</p>\n<h3 id=\"collectroutes\"><code>collectRoutes</code></h3>\n<p>Recursively collects emitted pages — every directory holding an\nindex.html is a servable route (dist is fully prerendered per route\nand per locale).</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>@param</code> {string} dir - directory to walk</li>\n<li><code>@returns</code> {string[]} route paths relative to dist ('/about/' style)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"en_fanout_re\"><code>EN_FANOUT_RE</code></h3>\n<p>Mechanical fan-out generators: the star-field dossier pages and the\nper-screenshot portfolio tour pages all instantiate one template with\ndifferent copy — a bounded sample covers the accessibility surface\nwithout an hours-long scan. Same for the docs portal's per-source-file\npages (one page per repo file).</p>\n<h3 id=\"docs_deep_re\"><code>DOCS_DEEP_RE</code></h3>\n<p>Deeper-than-section-landing docs portal pages (one page per repo file).</p>\n<h3 id=\"excluded_re\"><code>EXCLUDED_RE</code></h3>\n<p>Canonical exclusions: <code>/&lt;loc&gt;/…</code> locale trees and the <code>/langs/&lt;loc&gt;/</code>\nmirror are template translations of the EN surface — same DOM shapes,\ndifferent copy — and <code>/cms/…</code> is the auth-gated admin shell, not part\nof the public accessibility surface.</p>\n<h3 id=\"fanout_sample\"><code>FANOUT_SAMPLE</code></h3>\n<p>Routes per fan-out family kept for the canonical scope.</p>\n<h3 id=\"canonicalroutes\"><code>canonicalRoutes</code></h3>\n<p>Picks the canonical scan surface — English routes only, CMS excluded:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>every EN route scans, except fan-out families which contribute\na small deterministic sample (first N per family)</li>\n<li>docs portal depth-2 landings always scan; deeper per-source pages\ncontribute a sample</li>\n<li><code>@param</code> {string[]} routes every emitted route</li>\n<li><code>@returns</code> {string[]} canonical routes to scan</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"servedist\"><code>serveDist</code></h3>\n<p>Starts the loopback static server for dist/. Resolves with {server, base}.</p>\n</article>","mtime":"2026-10-22T08:58:26.452Z"}